Root cause:
The bug was caused by an improper handling of volume names in the function `RARVolNameToFirstName_BUGGED`. Specifically, the function did not adequately check if the provided string `s` was a valid RAR format or a specific type (NNN) before attempting to process it. This could lead to incorrect behavior or crashes when invalid volume names were passed to the function. The patch adds a check to ensure that the string is either a valid RAR format or a specific type before proceeding with further processing, thus improving the robustness of the volume consistency check.
